@page
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Contact us";
}
<article class="prose">
  <h1>Contact us</h1>
  <p class="lede">By “us,” we mean one person. The corporate headquarters is wherever
    the laptop is. The hold music is probably a kid asking when they get the ball.</p>

  <h2>You’ve reached the whole department</h2>
  <p>There’s no sales team, support desk or premium account manager. Huddle Board is
    a free app built for coaches and their kids. Everyone gets the whole thing,
    and everyone is welcome to help make it better.</p>

  <h2>GitHub is the front desk</h2>
  <p>Found a bug? Have an idea? Something confused your team at practice?
    <a href="https://github.com/crawfordjustin/huddle-board/issues">Open an issue on GitHub</a>.
    Tell us what happened, what you expected, and which device and browser you
    were using. A screenshot helps. Football terminology is welcome; a perfectly
    written bug report is optional.</p>
  <p>Check the existing issues first. Someone may already have spotted it, in which
    case you can add what you found. Replies happen when the person behind the
    front desk is back at the laptop.</p>

  <h2>The door is open</h2>
  <p>The code and play library are on
    <a href="https://github.com/crawfordjustin/huddle-board">GitHub</a> under the MIT
    license. Browse it, suggest a change, send a pull request, or make your own
    version for your team. You don’t have to write code to contribute: explaining
    what worked with real kids is useful too.</p>
  <p>Thanks for helping. We’ll tell the team. It’s a short meeting.</p>

  <p><a class="go big" href="https://github.com/crawfordjustin/huddle-board">Visit the GitHub repo</a></p>
</article>
